      "message": "In the commit message benchmarks, single-ref `sad 16x4` is `0.88x` (slower than SSE2 due to the 6 `vinserti32x4` row-packing shuffles + 512-bit horizontal reduction for a single iteration) and `sad 16x8/16x32/16x64` are `1.00x`. Should we skip specializing `aom_sad16x4` (or single-ref `aom_sad16xN` where there is no gain) for `avx512` and only enable `16xN` where it wins (`sad_avg`, `x3d`/`x4d`)?",
